<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia wage case ruling due next Tuesday - govt.</title>
<headline>Australia wage case ruling due next Tuesday - govt.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Industrial Relations Commission would hand down a ruling on the national &quot;living wage&quot; case next Tuesday, the office of Industrial Relations Minister Peter Reith said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A spokesman from the Industrial Relations Commission said its decision on the trade union movement's claim for a national wage rise would be handed down at 0400 GMT (2.00 p.m.) at the commission in Sydney.</p>
</text>
